# SemanticScript standard-library canonical module: standard.bit.

module standard.bit
purpose module standard.bit "Canonical standard-library module for bit operations."
moduleOwns standard.bit "The official import path `standard.bit` and this module's implementation body."
moduleDoesNotOwn standard.bit "App-specific wrappers, compatibility aliases, or generated build artifacts."
invariant module standard.bit "The standard module entry is this file; tests live beside it as `main.test.sem`."

exportConstant standard.bit bitModuleVersionText
storage module immutable bitModuleVersionText CNullTerminatedByteString "standard.bit 0.1"

# Canonical standard-library implementation body.
# ============================================================
# SEMANTICSCRIPT STANDARD LIBRARY: bitwise operations on CSignedInt64
# ============================================================
#
# rationale: each operation lowers to a single LLVM bitwise / shift
#   instruction through the math.* primitives shiftLeftI64 (shl),
#   shiftRightArithmeticI64 (ashr), shiftRightLogicalI64 (lshr),
#   bitwiseAndI64 (and), bitwiseOrI64 (or), bitwiseXorI64 (xor), and
#   bitwiseNotI64 (xor -1). The earlier revision emulated these with
#   O(bitIndex) multiply/divide-by-two loops; the primitives make every
#   operation O(1) and branchless.
#
# invariant: predicate / mutation ops operate on the true 64-bit
#   two's-complement pattern. isSignedInt64BitSet checks the k-th bit via
#   ((inputValue >> k) & 1) using a logical shift, so it is correct for
#   negative inputs (e.g. isSignedInt64BitSet(-1, k) == true for every
#   k in [0, 63]). set / clear / toggle preserve every other bit.
#
# security: pure value-level bit math; no allocation; no branches over
#   secret-dependent bit patterns.
#
# timing: O(1) per operation â€” one shift plus at most one logical op.
#
# observability: no logs, no metrics.
#
# warning: bitIndex must be in [0, 63]. A shift count >= 64 is LLVM
#   poison (undefined), not a wrap; callers must mask the index first.
#
# Operations exposed:
#   shiftSignedInt64BitsLeft(inputValue, bitIndex)   -> CSignedInt64
#   shiftSignedInt64BitsRight(inputValue, bitIndex)  -> CSignedInt64
#   isSignedInt64BitSet(inputValue, bitIndex)        -> Bool
#   setSignedInt64Bit(inputValue, bitIndex)          -> CSignedInt64
#   clearSignedInt64Bit(inputValue, bitIndex)        -> CSignedInt64
#   toggleSignedInt64Bit(inputValue, bitIndex)       -> CSignedInt64

# Pure-module file: smoke + extended tests live in
# std/bit/main.test.sem.

domainLiteral integerZeroComparisonValue CSignedInt64 0
domainLiteralTrust integerZeroComparisonValue trustedStaticLiteral
domainLiteral integerOneBitMaskSeed CSignedInt64 1
domainLiteralTrust integerOneBitMaskSeed trustedStaticLiteral

# section bit.shift

operation shiftSignedInt64BitsLeft
input operation shiftSignedInt64BitsLeft inputValue CSignedInt64
input operation shiftSignedInt64BitsLeft bitIndex CSignedInt64
output operation shiftSignedInt64BitsLeft CSignedInt64
memory shiftSignedInt64BitsLeft heap no
async shiftSignedInt64BitsLeft no
purpose operation shiftSignedInt64BitsLeft "Returns inputValue << bitIndex via a single LLVM shl."
invariant operation shiftSignedInt64BitsLeft "For bitIndex in [0, 63], equivalent to inputValue * 2^bitIndex modulo 2^64."
warning shiftSignedInt64BitsLeft "bitIndex must be in [0, 63]; a count >= 64 is LLVM poison (undefined)."
guarantee shiftSignedInt64BitsLeft "O(1) â€” one shl instruction."
label startShiftSignedInt64BitsLeft
call shiftLeftCall math.shiftLeftI64
argument shiftLeftCall left I64 inputValue
argument shiftLeftCall right I64 bitIndex
run shiftLeftCall
bind value shiftedLeftResult CSignedInt64 shiftLeftCall
return value shiftedLeftResult

operation shiftSignedInt64BitsRight
input operation shiftSignedInt64BitsRight inputValue CSignedInt64
input operation shiftSignedInt64BitsRight bitIndex CSignedInt64
output operation shiftSignedInt64BitsRight CSignedInt64
memory shiftSignedInt64BitsRight heap no
async shiftSignedInt64BitsRight no
purpose operation shiftSignedInt64BitsRight "Returns inputValue >> bitIndex via a single LLVM ashr (arithmetic / sign-propagating)."
invariant operation shiftSignedInt64BitsRight "Arithmetic shift: matches C's `>>` on signed operands â€” floor-divides toward minus-infinity, replicating the sign bit into the vacated high bits."
warning shiftSignedInt64BitsRight "bitIndex must be in [0, 63]; a count >= 64 is LLVM poison. Use a logical right shift (math.shiftRightLogicalI64) when the sign bit should not propagate."
guarantee shiftSignedInt64BitsRight "O(1) â€” one ashr instruction."
label startShiftSignedInt64BitsRight
call shiftRightCall math.shiftRightArithmeticI64
argument shiftRightCall left I64 inputValue
argument shiftRightCall right I64 bitIndex
run shiftRightCall
bind value shiftedRightResult CSignedInt64 shiftRightCall
return value shiftedRightResult

# section bit.predicate

operation isSignedInt64BitSet
input operation isSignedInt64BitSet inputValue CSignedInt64
input operation isSignedInt64BitSet bitIndex CSignedInt64
output operation isSignedInt64BitSet Bool
memory isSignedInt64BitSet heap no
async isSignedInt64BitSet no
purpose operation isSignedInt64BitSet "Returns true when the k-th bit of inputValue is set, equivalent to ((inputValue >> bitIndex) & 1) != 0."
invariant operation isSignedInt64BitSet "Pure function over the two's-complement bit pattern; correct for negative inputs because the shift is logical."
guarantee isSignedInt64BitSet "Total. O(1)."
label startIsSignedInt64BitSet
call shiftDownToTargetBitCall math.shiftRightLogicalI64
argument shiftDownToTargetBitCall left I64 inputValue
argument shiftDownToTargetBitCall right I64 bitIndex
run shiftDownToTargetBitCall
bind value shiftedDownInput CSignedInt64 shiftDownToTargetBitCall
call extractLowBitCall math.bitwiseAndI64
argument extractLowBitCall left I64 shiftedDownInput
argument extractLowBitCall right I64 integerOneBitMaskSeed
run extractLowBitCall
bind value lowestBitValue I64 extractLowBitCall
call detectLowBitIsOneCall math.notEqualI64
argument detectLowBitIsOneCall left I64 lowestBitValue
argument detectLowBitIsOneCall right I64 integerZeroComparisonValue
run detectLowBitIsOneCall
bind value lowBitIsOne Bool detectLowBitIsOneCall
return value lowBitIsOne

# section bit.mutation

operation setSignedInt64Bit
input operation setSignedInt64Bit inputValue CSignedInt64
input operation setSignedInt64Bit bitIndex CSignedInt64
output operation setSignedInt64Bit CSignedInt64
memory setSignedInt64Bit heap no
async setSignedInt64Bit no
purpose operation setSignedInt64Bit "Returns inputValue with the k-th bit forced to 1, computed as inputValue OR (1 << bitIndex). No change if the bit is already set."
invariant operation setSignedInt64Bit "isSignedInt64BitSet(setSignedInt64Bit(x, k), k) == true; every other bit is preserved."
guarantee setSignedInt64Bit "Total. O(1) â€” branchless OR with a single-bit mask."
label startSetSignedInt64Bit
call buildSetMaskCall math.shiftLeftI64
argument buildSetMaskCall left I64 integerOneBitMaskSeed
argument buildSetMaskCall right I64 bitIndex
run buildSetMaskCall
bind value setBitMask CSignedInt64 buildSetMaskCall
call applySetMaskCall math.bitwiseOrI64
argument applySetMaskCall left I64 inputValue
argument applySetMaskCall right I64 setBitMask
run applySetMaskCall
bind value setBitResultValue CSignedInt64 applySetMaskCall
return value setBitResultValue

operation clearSignedInt64Bit
input operation clearSignedInt64Bit inputValue CSignedInt64
input operation clearSignedInt64Bit bitIndex CSignedInt64
output operation clearSignedInt64Bit CSignedInt64
memory clearSignedInt64Bit heap no
async clearSignedInt64Bit no
purpose operation clearSignedInt64Bit "Returns inputValue with the k-th bit forced to 0, computed as inputValue AND NOT(1 << bitIndex). No change if the bit is already clear."
invariant operation clearSignedInt64Bit "isSignedInt64BitSet(clearSignedInt64Bit(x, k), k) == false; every other bit is preserved."
guarantee clearSignedInt64Bit "Total. O(1) â€” branchless AND with an inverted single-bit mask."
label startClearSignedInt64Bit
call buildClearMaskCall math.shiftLeftI64
argument buildClearMaskCall left I64 integerOneBitMaskSeed
argument buildClearMaskCall right I64 bitIndex
run buildClearMaskCall
bind value clearBitMask CSignedInt64 buildClearMaskCall
call invertClearMaskCall math.bitwiseNotI64
argument invertClearMaskCall value I64 clearBitMask
run invertClearMaskCall
bind value invertedClearMask CSignedInt64 invertClearMaskCall
call applyClearMaskCall math.bitwiseAndI64
argument applyClearMaskCall left I64 inputValue
argument applyClearMaskCall right I64 invertedClearMask
run applyClearMaskCall
bind value clearBitResultValue CSignedInt64 applyClearMaskCall
return value clearBitResultValue

operation toggleSignedInt64Bit
input operation toggleSignedInt64Bit inputValue CSignedInt64
input operation toggleSignedInt64Bit bitIndex CSignedInt64
output operation toggleSignedInt64Bit CSignedInt64
memory toggleSignedInt64Bit heap no
async toggleSignedInt64Bit no
purpose operation toggleSignedInt64Bit "Returns inputValue with the k-th bit flipped, computed as inputValue XOR (1 << bitIndex)."
invariant operation toggleSignedInt64Bit "Self-inverse: toggleSignedInt64Bit(toggleSignedInt64Bit(x, k), k) == x; every other bit is preserved."
guarantee toggleSignedInt64Bit "Total. O(1) â€” branchless XOR with a single-bit mask."
label startToggleSignedInt64Bit
call buildToggleMaskCall math.shiftLeftI64
argument buildToggleMaskCall left I64 integerOneBitMaskSeed
argument buildToggleMaskCall right I64 bitIndex
run buildToggleMaskCall
bind value toggleBitMask CSignedInt64 buildToggleMaskCall
call applyToggleMaskCall math.bitwiseXorI64
argument applyToggleMaskCall left I64 inputValue
argument applyToggleMaskCall right I64 toggleBitMask
run applyToggleMaskCall
bind value toggleBitResultValue CSignedInt64 applyToggleMaskCall
return value toggleBitResultValue
